  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Lean season emergency WASH and Health response in Monguno.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe proposed actions aim to improve the availability, access, and utilisation of essential health and&#xa0;WASH&#xa0;services, reaching 18,784 of the most vulnerable IDPs and Host community members in Monguno. Specifically, the action will contribute to reduced morbidity and mortality by providing life-saving integrated health and&#xa0;WASH&#xa0;services. The proposed action will result in:ltbrgtlt/pgtltpgtltbrgt1. Improved access to integrated primary health care, comprehensive sexual  reproductive health care, and disease surveillance and outbreak response within IDP and host community settlements in Monguno.lt/pgtltpgt2.&#xa0;Increased consumption of safe drinking water to meet the domestic needs of 14,400 individuals (viii). Improved access to safe and adequate sanitation facilities by at-risk IDPs and host community individuals.lt/pgtltpgt3. Improved knowledge and adoption of positive hygiene practices in targeted locations.lt/pgtltpgtThe project will be implemented by a consortium led by ZOA in partnership with LPF. LPF will be the consortium lead for Health and ZOA, providing technical expertise in WASH and overall grants  oversight leadership. This action, which focuses on the lean season, will also serve as a response and anticipatory action instrument to protect and prevent the deterioration of the humanitarian crisis into catastrophic levels, in line with the HNRP 2025 priorities. ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
